        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "83e7e253-7bd8-569b-ab0d-a612c23bf0d4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: \"Prostitute\", \"Chinese Democracy\"\n- People: Axl Rose, Paul Tobias, Robin Finck\n- Organizations: Guns N' Roses, Nine Inch Nails, Spin, VH1\n- Topics: songwriting, hard rock rankings\n\nFacts:\n- Robin Finck was born on November 7, 1971, and he is an American guitarist.\n- The song \"Prostitute\" existed by at least July 1999, when Spin reported that Axl Rose was working on a song with the working title \"Prostitute,\" according to Youth.\n- \"Prostitute\" was written by Axl Rose and Paul Tobias, with additional work by Robin Finck.\n- Guns N' Roses released its sixth studio album, \"Chinese Democracy,\" in 2008.\n- \"Prostitute\" is the fourteenth and final track on Guns N' Roses' 2008 album \"Chinese Democracy.\"\n- Robin Finck played in Nine Inch Nails and Guns N' Roses, two bands that VH1 included in its \"100 Greatest Artists of Hard Rock\" ranking at no. 43 and no. 9 respectively.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "125ddeb7-59f6-5bd2-89db-fa5a50ae41b9",
        "text": "Page: Prostitute (song). Sentence: \"Prostitute\" is the fourteenth and final track from \"Chinese Democracy\", Guns N' Roses' sixth studio album released in 2008.\nPage: Prostitute (song). Sentence: The song dates back to at least 1999, as it was mentioned in a July issue of \"Spin\" Magazine; \"\"Rose is laboring over a song with the working title 'Prostitute', according to Youth, but past successes weigh heavily on him...\"\" The song is written by Axl Rose and Paul Tobias with additional work by Robin Finck.\nPage: Robin Finck. Sentence: Robert John \"Robin\" Finck (born November 7, 1971) is an American guitarist.\nPage: Robin Finck. Sentence: He is one of only a few artists who has played in two different bands listed on VH1's \"100 Greatest Artists of Hard Rock\": Nine Inch Nails (ranked no. 43) and Guns N' Roses (ranked no. 9).",
